    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0444102c-1dd3-36df-9a97-1558a54ac379",
                "word": "midsentence",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                        "entry_id": "0444102c-1dd3-36df-9a97-1558a54ac379",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Occurring in the middle of a sentence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6aede6e-b96d-4b14-b189-49b6afda23a7",
                                "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                                "text": "In neither case was there an effect on comprehension as measured by the subjects’ free recall. Subjects recalled as much with midsentence interruptions as with end-of-sentence interruptions as with no interruptions at all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19c20b6d-3dc6-4b6a-b3b4-d50279bb2a1a",
                                "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                                "text": "Instead of pausing after each sentence, Dr. King stopped briefly after each refrain of “Let freedom ring,” building intensity and creating the musical effect of a crescendo. His midsentence pauses emphasized the repeating pattern in his examples and let the audience know what to expect next."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "803af9a7-2614-41d2-b9f4-c5531eb56868",
                                "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                                "text": "Paul carefully safeguards the priority of divine initiative over human efforts to come into relationship with God. Perhaps the most striking illustration of this is his midsentence self-correction in 4:9: “Now, however, that you have come to know God, or rather to be known by God . . .”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e464f299-afd8-4206-8c37-3e075a96501a",
                                "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                                "text": "“You again,” Karp growled. He gestured to Guma, making hand signals to get a trace going on the call. Guma quit his midsentence comeback aimed at Stupenagel and hurried from the room."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f4ad42d-0177-4a68-b766-34e4b2667ab2",
                                "sense_id": "f3d2936a-eb77-3089-8bf5-0e7f58a1d67d",
                                "text": "“Mr. Borovsky only makes deals through his—” Ovechkin broke off. Quinn’s brow lowered, puzzled by his midsentence stoppage."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "df910e0f-f47f-34de-a412-c9bff9df509f",
                "word": "midsentence",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4927c8d-5674-3084-875f-772347ac598b",
                        "entry_id": "df910e0f-f47f-34de-a412-c9bff9df509f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the middle of a sentence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "844f09ec-c0c8-4470-aa8a-6dc7fe885a32",
                                "sense_id": "d4927c8d-5674-3084-875f-772347ac598b",
                                "text": "“At least I believe in something! You’re nothing but a typical godless American with no values and . . .” Chad interrupted midsentence: “You don’t like the way I am?[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fe23ac7-beac-47e7-8b02-3bd2e7b68f12",
                                "sense_id": "d4927c8d-5674-3084-875f-772347ac598b",
                                "text": "With Juju Jackson there was never a warning or an explanation. Jackson could pull a gun or a knife, shoot and maim someone midsentence during a conversation that seemed perfectly reasonable, even pleasant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "965b690c-e0fd-4975-a5a5-f9f4cf168251",
                                "sense_id": "d4927c8d-5674-3084-875f-772347ac598b",
                                "text": "Stop someone midsentence if he or she is in your presence or write if he or she is not. These throwaway lines about age are detrimental and damaging."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d4046aa9-254e-3ec8-b2d1-98794d065e5a",
                "word": "midsentence",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                        "entry_id": "d4046aa9-254e-3ec8-b2d1-98794d065e5a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The middle of a sentence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b9a6c34-ed58-438d-b35a-496a8a014bfc",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "I mean this man starts his day with both feet moving, without a dab of anxiety, with him saying, “Okay, ready!” He can fall asleep in midsentence, in his midsentence, and then go without a toss or a tumble or a single concern for the next seven hours."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebbc22ae-fd67-4c2c-8d3c-14b4aa1dadec",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "He talked into the receiver. “Sure, I read all about it this morning. I wondered whether—” As he spoke, he reached out and pushed down on the button, breaking the connection in his midsentence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e771c37f-3e6f-4dda-b144-a58a7ebfccc8",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "But the narrative broke off in midsentence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c913e23b-b668-49c0-a2b6-132af4909778",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "Chief Justice Rehnquist was famous for cutting off lawyers in midsentence, even midsyllable, as soon as the red light on the lectern came on to signal that time was up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "29af57a4-1869-410a-bc57-f53e53c7980e",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "Gerbert de Montreuil picks up in the midsentence of the Second Continuation, and Manessier writes the Third Continuation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e15cde8-4f3b-4bf4-870a-78c277b51a76",
                                "sense_id": "08404ba2-ec41-3964-beaf-8c39b0793eb0",
                                "text": "He died, in the midsentence of his life, as these books were being published."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
